  "verses": {
    "verse": [
      [
        "Angels we have heard on high",
        "sweetly singing o'er the plains,",
        "and the mountains in reply",
        "echoing their joyous strains."
      ],
      [
        "Shepherds, why this jubilee?",
        "Why your joyous strains prolong?",
        "What the gladsome tidings be",
        "which inspire your heavenly song?"
      ],
      [
        "Come to Bethlehem and see",
        "Him whose birth the angels sing;",
        "come, adore on bended knee",
        "Christ the Lord, the newborn King."
      ],
      [
        "See Him in a manger laid,",
        "whom the choirs of angels praise;",
        "Mary, Joseph, lend your aid,",
        "while our hearts in love we raise."
      ]
    ]
  },
  "arrangerNotes": "Verified against the LilyPond score on English Wikipedia; the repeats and first/second endings are written out. No simplification needed. Range low 5 to 6. C and D arrangements use identical degree sequences (both fit their drums). Lyrics of the added verses: Verses 2–4: the 19th-century English text (after James Chadwick, 1862) as given on English Wikipedia (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angels_We_Have_Heard_on_High). The 'Gloria' refrain is sung after every verse.",
  "verified": true
